[[!meta title="Upgrading the GNOME Software backport"]]

[[!toc levels=2]]

# First time setup

    git clone git@gitlab-ssh.tails.net:tails/gnome-software
    cd gnome-software
    git remote add debian-upstream https://salsa.debian.org/gnome-team/gnome-software.git

# Import new version

First make sure your checkout is up-to-date:

    git fetch origin
    git fetch debian-upstream

Let's say GNOME Software 51.1-1 hits Debian unstable, then set:

    DEBIAN_TAG=debian/51.1-1
    TAILS_ISSUE=12345

And derive these:

    VERSION="${DEBIAN_TAG#*/}"~bpo13+0tails1
    GNOME_SOFTWARE_BRANCH="tails/backport-${DEBIAN_TAG:?}"
    TAILS_BRANCH="${TAILS_ISSUE:?}-gnome-software-${DEBIAN_TAG#*/}-backport"

## Check for new Adwaita usage

GNOME Software 51 depends on `libadwaita` >= 1.8~alpha, but Trixie
only has 1.7.6, and we don't want to backport a higher
version. Therefore we have to monitor any changes we introduce with
new version for new usage of `libadwaita`, and make sure it still
works. As an example of something that does *not* work, but which we
considers acceptable, [commit
657bc3aa](https://gitlab.tails.net/tails/gnome-software/-/commit/657bc3aaa2a6a44bd3768abae3edfb53979ab6bb)
introduces
[AdwShortcutsSection](https://gnome.pages.gitlab.gnome.org/libadwaita/doc/1.8/class.ShortcutsSection.html)
which requires `libadwaita` >= 1.8, so in our backport this dialog
doesn't work. For details, see [this
thread](https://gitlab.tails.net/tails/gnome-software/-/merge_requests/1#note_291825).

    git log -p -GAdw origin/tails/trixie.."${DEBIAN_TAG:?}" -- src

## Prepare new release

    git checkout -b "${GNOME_SOFTWARE_BRANCH:?}" origin/tails/trixie
    git merge "${DEBIAN_TAG:?}"

You likely will have to deal with merge conflicts in
`debian/changelog`.

Then prepare the release:

    (
    set -eu -o pipefail
    gbp dch --new-version="${VERSION:?}" --distribution="${TAILS_BRANCH:?}" --ignore-branch
    dch --append "Rebuild for Trixie"
    git commit -m "releasing package gnome-software version ${VERSION}" debian/changelog
    gbp buildpackage --git-tag-only --git-sign-tags --git-ignore-branch
    git show
    )

# Build

For instance, if you use `pbuilder`:

    gbp buildpackage --git-ignore-branch --git-pbuilder --git-arch=amd64 --git-dist=trixie

Before uploading the packages, remember to create `${TAILS_BRANCH}` in
`tails.git` so the required APT suite is created.

# Publish

    git push \
        --set-upstream \
        -o merge_request.create \
        -o merge_request.draft \
        -o merge_request.target=tails/trixie \
        -o merge_request.title="Draft: Backport ${DEBIAN_TAG}" \
        origin "${GNOME_SOFTWARE_BRANCH:?}"
